 "visual": "Routes: San Francisco, Asia, Australia all passing near Hawaii.",
 "texto": "Look where Hawaii sits. Halfway between America and Asia, alone in the biggest ocean on Earth. In the age of sailing ships and steamships, every long voyage across the Pacific needed a place to stop for water, food and coal. Hawaii was that place. Whaling ships from New England turned Honolulu and Lahaina into some of the busiest ports in the Pacific.",
